* Add a Lua rule format in which rules are Lua scripts returning a rule table,
  with every official rule shipped in both formats, and select the engine with
  the new -e/--engine option - the historic YAML engine stays, deprecated, for
  the transition.
* Add a Lua configuration file format, considered when no YAML configuration
  file is found, whose scripts run with arara's own values in scope.
* Make the invocation a set of projects: .proj.lua files declare their files,
  priorities, dependencies and working directories, specifications merge into
  one ordered run, and loose files ride as the anonymous project.
* Add the -c/--console option and the console configuration key, choosing
  between the plain presentation and the styled one, which carries live
  feedback while a task runs.
* Let the log file trail the session's every mutation, and name the verdict and
  the provenance of the run.

See the full changelog of this release at
